EXT. THE SALTY BISCUIT - FISHING BOAT - DAWN

Calm sea. Pink sky. A little wooden boat bobbing like a bath toy.

CAPTAIN PIP
(polishing the brass compass with their sleeve, not looking up)
Nobody touch the net. Nobody even think about the net.

MARLO
(a crab, hiding behind a bucket, tapping the net with one claw)
I'm not thinking about it. I'm just... standing near it.

CAPTAIN PIP
(without turning)
Thinking loudly.

Silence.

Gulls. Far away.

BERNIE
(a seagull, landing on the rail with a flap, a fish in their beak that is clearly not theirs)
Morning, Captain! Lovely morning for a completely innocent morning.

CAPTAIN PIP
(raising one eyebrow at the fish)
Bernie.

BERNIE
(swallowing it whole)
What fish?

Nothing.

OLLIE
(a brass lantern hanging from the mast, swinging, lighting up and dimming as they speak)
Captain. The sea is humming again.

CAPTAIN PIP
(finally setting down the compass, listening)
Hm.

Waves. Slap, slap.

OLLIE
(whispering)
It only hums when something's coming.

NINA
(a girl of nine, in a yellow raincoat, climbing up from below deck with a mug)
Cocoa's ready. Who wants cocoa?

MARLO
(from behind the bucket, hopeful)
Me.

BERNIE ^
(at the same time, wings out)
Me!

NINA
(handing the mug to Captain Pip first, steady, careful not to spill)
Captain gets the first sip. That's the rule.

CAPTAIN PIP
(taking it, holding it with both hands, a very small smile)
That's the rule.

A bubble rises beside the boat. Pop. Another. Pop.

OLLIE
(flickering low)
It's here.

Everyone freezes. Even the gull.

NINA
(very quietly, tucking her hand into the Captain's coat pocket)
Is it a big one?

CAPTAIN PIP
(sipping, eyes on the water)
Biggest I've ever seen.

Rain.

No. Just spray.

MARLO
(creeping out from behind the bucket, claws up)
Should we run?

CAPTAIN PIP
(setting the mug on the rail)
We should say hello.

The water rises, slow and glassy, a long blue curve.

Silence.
